  "obsidian" in servers;` line. Drop the `if (hasBrain && hasObsidian)`
  branch entirely. Drop the `if (hasObsidian)` legacy-migration
  branch entirely. After the edit, the function reads only
  `servers.brain` and ignores any other keys present in
  `mcpServers`. The presence of an `obsidian` key in the user's
  `.mcp.json` is no longer this module's concern; sync owns
  `.mcp.json` writes and only writes the `brain` key.

