  in the implementor's head against the spec's "Step 1 / Step 2 /
  ... / Step 7" worked good-example block. Confirm: step 1 is
  `would-create` with the bundled template bytes; step 2 is
  `would-skip` (path slot null); steps 3-6 are `would-skip` (same
  reason); step 7 is `would-create` with prescription args carrying
  null verbatim at the path-slot index. The names, categories, and
  filePaths line up with the spec.

- [ ] 6b. Manually trace a self-heal pass (per the spec's "Self-heal
  scenario" block). Setup: brain.aide on disk with path slot filled,
